    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can offer step-by-step explanations in simple language, like a tutor. They can adapt to different learning styles and give instant feedback. For students, this makes maths less intimidating. In schools, they can help teachers create personalized lessons. It’s not magic—it’s a tool to make learning more accessible and patient."
